# Weed.com content production (Learn / Layer 1)

## Rank Math (publish)

- **Weed.com** (`WP_TOOL_SCOPE.weedComContentProduction`): Rank Math **focus keyword** is set from the **WordPress post title** (trimmed, max 191 chars), with fallback to the first editorial keyword if the title is empty. See `rankMathFocusKeywordFromTitle` in `lib/contentProduction/publishPost.ts`.
- **Other scopes** (e.g. green.org): focus keyword uses **`pickFocusKeyphrase`** (first keyword, else title snippet) for Rank Math.

## Expert Insight — Contentenator (Layer 1, before Dr. Tabibi / Layer 2)

All Layer 1 Weed.com Learn prompts live in `weedLayer1BiblePrompt()` in `lib/contentProduction/generateContentPost.ts` (Bible v7+). Before any draft goes to human or Dr. Tabibi review, the model must enforce:

1. **Study-type accuracy** — Words like trial, RCT, review, meta-analysis, cohort, etc. must match the **actual** publication type on PubMed for the cited PMID.
2. **PMID verification** — Every PMID must resolve to the **same** paper as the expert-cite line; no invented, guessed, or unrelated PMIDs.
3. **Claim-to-citation match** — Specific findings (doses, outcomes, effect language) must be supported by **that** PMID, not by a primary study only discussed inside a cited review.

When editing the Bible string, keep these three gates aligned with the **CONTENTENATOR** section, **CITATIONS**, and **QUALITY SELF-CHECK** blocks in the same file. Also mirror key points in `brandAddendumForScope` (weed) and the Weed branch of the generate-content `userMessage` where applicable.

## Tabibi Gold Standard citation JSON (Expert Insight PMID source)

- **Data file:** `lib/data/tabibiPmidDatabaseCwV6.json` (Tabibi library: metadata + `pmid_database` array).
- **Selection:** `selectRelevantTabibiEntries()` in `lib/tabibiPmidDatabase.ts` scores entries against title, keywords, editorial brief, content angle, and product type; returns up to 14 candidates (tier tie-break: T1 first). If nothing matches, it falls back to tier-prioritized entries.
- **Prompt:** `buildTabibiLibraryUserBlock()` injects the **TABIBI GOLD STANDARD CITATION LIBRARY** block into the generate-content user message for Weed only. The model must cite **only** PMIDs from that list in Expert Insight and Sources (at most 3 per article per Bible).
- **API:** Successful Weed responses may include `tabibiExpertInsightPmidsSuggested` (ranked pool) and `tabibiSourcesFooterPmids` (PMIDs actually written into the appended Sources block, up to 4).
- **Sources footer:** `appendTabibiSourcesFooter()` in `lib/tabibiSourcesFooter.ts` runs after `finalizeWeedLearnHtml` + `lockExpertBoxTypography`. It inserts a Bible-style **Sources** block (JSON-backed citations only) before the legal footer, strips a duplicate model-generated Sources section when it matches the Bible outer wrapper, and picks PMIDs via `pickTabibiSourcesForFooter()` (prefer PMIDs linked in the HTML, then pad with the next most relevant ranked entries; max 4).

## Expert Insight HTML hook and typography

- The outer wrapper of each Expert Insight block must keep **`class="expert-box"`** on the green panel `<div>` (see Bible template in `weedLayer1BiblePrompt`). Themes can target `.expert-box` for extra CSS; inline styles remain the Layer 1 default.
- **Inside `.expert-box` only:** every text element must use **`font-family: Inter,sans-serif!important`** on its inline `style` (Inter plus the generic `sans-serif` keyword; `!important` beats pasted Word spans and many theme rules). Do not use `system-ui`, `-apple-system`, `Segoe UI`, `Roboto`, or other named stacks — including on the PMID `<a>`. Publish/generate runs `lockExpertBoxTypography` in `lib/postHtml.ts` to strip foreign `font-family` / `font` inside each `.expert-box` and re-apply the Inter lock on every opening tag.
